From 4c92831c09677b56c08f8de41e811c48fcefeeee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XZNON <noreply@local>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:36:01 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Style aspect: detect dithering on art-pixel centres,
 measure every sampled frame, steadier colour scenes

Dithering:
- frame_texture now reads one sample per art pixel at the cell centres (art_pixels), phase-aligned
  to the grid: _lock refines the period per axis near the shot's period and finds the cell-border
  offset from the hard-edge profile (largest Fourier term). The old INTER_AREA resize at a
  non-integer period (2.667 px at 480 wide) blended neighbouring cells and erased checkerboards.
- dither_share counts 2x2 checkerboards on brightness (video coding blurs colour more), with the
  two diagonals one tone each, and only next to another checkerboard window (lone matches are chance).
- Per shot: dither (median) plus dither_peak and per-frame dither; per video: dither (weighted
  median), dither_peak, and dither_frames (time share of sampled frames above DITHER_ON = 0.03,
  picked from the reference: no-dither frames 0-0.02, dithered band seams 0.035-0.15, a dithered
  shadow 0.1-0.4). style.md says "checkerboard dithering in N% of frames, up to X%".

Colour scenes:
- ShotCtx gains all_frames (every sampled frame, defaults to frames), filled in measure_shot; the
  style aspect measures all of them instead of the ~6 picked frames (which also covered only the
  first two thirds of each shot). Other aspects are unchanged.
- After a cut a frame joins the current scene only when it matches the scene as a whole, so a fade
  to white no longer carries the white shot after it along.
- A scene of one frame or under SCENE_MIN (1 s) inside a shot joins the closer neighbour in the same
  shot (or both, when they match across it); a short scene holding a whole shot stays.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
